From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:03:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] android: probe the platform EGL display for GPU SoftISP

Adapt haretic's Android EGL display selection to the upstream renderer.
Use Android's default EGL display instead of the Linux surfaceless
platform entry point, retaining upstream's GLES context initialization.

Do not copy MediaTek DMA formats, Rabbit shaders or device-specific
image processing.

Base-commit: df8e348d64b4932a0676256ed24f0da3ee9438bc
Source: https://github.com/haretic/android_external_libcamera/commit/507821791c091bdbb9ef782c651c82d65b9dc511
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/egl.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/egl.cpp
@@ -315,9 +315,14 @@
 {
 	EGLDisplay display;
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+	/* Android selects its EGL implementation through the default display. */
+	display = eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY);
+#else
 	display = eglGetPlatformDisplay(EGL_PLATFORM_SURFACELESS_MESA,
 					EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY,
 					nullptr);
+#endif
 
 	if (display == EGL_NO_DISPLAY) {
 		LOG(eGL, Info) << "Unable to get EGL display";
